# OpenClaw — Product Vision & Positioning

## What OpenClaw IS

OpenClaw is a **factory framework** that empowers organizations to spin up their own AI workforces.

The platform handles:
- Model training pipeline (RAG adaptation, FAISS, eval harness)
- Multi-tenant Model Forge (workspaces, datasets, jobs, registry, deployments)
- Governance layer (human-in-loop, audit trace, privilege warnings)
- Benchmark integration (adversarial playbook, multi-LLM testing)
- ZOA, Archon, Kairos execution engines
- Skill generation, validation, and catalog

Organizations use OpenClaw to spin up their own AI SaaS products. We are the factory. They are the product.

## What OpenClaw is NOT

- NOT a legal API product
- NOT a law firm tool
- NOT a single-vertical SaaS
- NOT a chatbot wrapper

## The Law Firm Vertical

The law firm / legal AI operating layer is the **first proof-of-concept vertical** to validate the repeatable framework. It demonstrates:
- A complete training pipeline (CUAD dataset → FAISS → eval → registry → deployment)
- Governance envelope (human review required, privilege warnings, audit trace)
- Multi-agent routing (intake → specialist agents)
- Playbook harness (10 scenarios, v1/v2 eval)

Every future vertical (IR, marketing, HR, biotech, finance) runs on **identical infrastructure** with different skill bundles installed.

## The Core Insight

> Every vertical is just a bundle of skills + a knowledge graph + a playbook.
> The platform never knows what industry it's serving.

A law firm and a VC fund and a biotech all run on the same infrastructure. They just have different skill bundles installed.

## Positioning Language

Use this language in all UI copy, landing pages, and documentation:

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| "Legal AI API" | "AI workforce factory" |
| "Law firm tool" | "First proof-of-concept vertical" |
| "Demo" | "Live" or "Production" |
| "API endpoints" | "Deployed AI workforce" |
| "Legal SaaS" | "SaaS-as-a-Service factory" |
| "Our product" | "Your AI workforce" |

## The Three Moats

1. **Skill ecosystem** — 791+ real skills from GitHub, 5,400+ on ClawHub. Pre-install domain-specific packs on tenant provision.
2. **Governance layer** — human-in-loop, audit trail, privilege warnings baked into every output. Not optional.
3. **Repeatable factory** — any vertical spins up in one click. Law firm today, biotech tomorrow, VC fund next week.

